s\n108:     role: adapter\n109:     Translates:\n110:       - external provider JSON protocol envelopes\n111:       - Oulipoly typed provider client DTOs\n112:   - component: crates/oulipoly-provider/src/process.rs\n113:     role: adapter\n114:     Translates:\n115:       - provider subprocess lifecycle contract\n116:       - Oulipoly process identity observer contract\n117:   - component: crates/oulipoly-runtime/src/executor/external_provider/request_builder.rs\n118:     role: adapter\n119:     Translates:\n120:       - Oulipoly model/provider dispatch context\n121:       - external provider policy.evaluate and launch request JSON contracts\n122:   - component: crates/oulipoly-runtime/src/executor/external_provider/launch_result_mapper.rs\n123:     role: adapter\n124:     Translates:\n125:       - external provider LaunchExit event stream/session metadata\n126:       - Oulipoly runtime execution result and session capture fields\n127:   - component: crates/oulipoly-runtime/src/executor/external_provider/dispatch.rs\n128:     role: adapter\n129:     Translates:\n130:       - Oulipoly executor dispatch contract\n131:       - external provider policy/launch client contract\n132:       - sidecar process identity capture contract\n133:   - component: src-tauri/src/mailbox_delivery.rs\n134:     role: adapter\n135:     Translates:\n136:       - sidecar mailbox notification rows\n137:       - provider resume prompt and submitted-turn marker contract\n138:       - mailbox delivery confirmation status\n139:   - component: src-tauri/src/run/resume/orchestration.rs\n140:     role: adapter\n141:     Translates:\n142:       - resolved resume targets\n143:       - external provider start-known-session launch requests\n144:       - mailbox delivery confirmation and retry outcomes\n145:       - legacy CLI resume requests when no provider ref is present\n146:   - component: src-tauri/src/wake_coordinator.rs\n147:     role: adapter\n148:     Translates:\n149:       - agent-messenger notification requests\n150:       - PTY delivery control socket contract\n151:       - headless detached wake command contract\n152:       - sidecar mailbox wake claims\n153:   - component: src-tauri/tests/s11_external_provider_wake.rs\n154:     role: adapter\n155:     Translates:\n156:       - external provider script fixture contract\n157:       - CLI launch/notify/wake/resume integration surface\n158:       - sidecar mailbox and invocation result assertions\n159: ```\n160: \n161: ## Intrinsic-surface declarations\n162: \n163: ```yaml\n164: intrinsic_surface_declarations:\n165:   - component: crates/oulipoly-state/src/mailbox.rs\n166:     role: intrinsic-surface\n167:     Domain: sidecar_mailbox_delivery_state\n168:     Owns:\n169:       - mailbox pending/delivered/failed rows\n170:       - delivery_attempts and delivery_error updates\n171:       - wake claims and sidecar session runtime metadata\n172:   - component: crates/oulipoly-runtime/src/executor/cli/spawn_identity.rs\n173:     role: intrinsic-surface\n174:     Domain: external_provider_process_identity\n175:     Owns:\n176:       - provider child PID identity observation\n177:       - sidecar owner/session backfill\n178:       - launch-time sidecar identity validation\n179:   - component: crates/oulipoly-state/src/db.rs\n180:     role: intrinsic-surface\n181:     Domain: existing_session_turn_lookup\n182:     Owns:\n183:       - session_turns body lookup\n184:       - exact user text match predicate\n185: ```\n186: \n187: ## Test-harness declarations\n188: \n189: ```yaml\n190: test_harness_declarations:\n191:   - component: src-tauri/tests/s11_external_provider_wake.rs\n192:     role: test-harness\n193:     Surface:\n194:       - isolated XDG config/data/cache fixture directories\n195:       - external provider Python script fixture\n196:       - CLI launch, notify, wake, and resume commands\n197:       - sidecar pid-identity and mailbox row assertions\n198:       - submitted-turn marker positive and negative assertions\n199:   - component: src-tauri/tests/wu_b_mailbox_integration.rs\n200:     role: test-harness\n201:     Surface:\n202:       - mailbox notification and resume integration fixture\n203:       - exact ingested turn confirmation assertions\n204:       - mailbox batch and ordering assertions\n205:   - component: crates/oulipoly-runtime/tests/age217_s6a_policy_launch_dispatch.rs\n206:     role: test-harness\n207:     Surface:\n208:       - external provider policy/launch fake provider\n209:       - request and environment capture assertions\n210: ```\n211: \n212: No `state.db` schema migration is declared or required by this gate. The sidecar mailbox database owns the new delivery-attempt metadata used by S11.\n\n(End of file - total 212 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"# S11 Gate Contract\n\n## Component declared roles\n\nComponent: external provider wake delivery confirmation and detached resume continuity.\n\nDeclared roles: `orchestration`, `accessor`, `mapper`, `filter`, `validator`, `predicate`, `formatter`, `parser`.\n\n## Source scope\n\nThe functional S11 cutoff is `95699d6..1593ef8`. The audited net source range is `95699d6..1e043d3` because `1593ef8` left `scripts/opencode-turns` tracked as non-executable, which made the workspace test suite fail in `age243_s7a_session_dispatch`. The only remaining `1593ef8..1e043d3` source delta is `mode change 100644 => 100755 scripts/opencode-turns`; `2b7ab03` content is reverted and not part of the net source behavior.\n\n`crates/oulipoly-provider/src/generated.rs` receives no generated-artifact exemption. It is treated as hand-maintained provider protocol DTO code for this gate, consistent with the S10B disposition.\n\nTouched files in scope are exactly `planning/s11-gate/gates/touched-files.txt`.\n\n## Touched-file roles\n\n| File | Declared roles | Role notes |\n|---|---|---|","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/home/nes/projects/agent-runner/worktrees/age-pid-sidecar